ight singular vectors of $A,$ i.e., the unit eigenvectors of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that the singular values are ${\\sigma }_{1}=5$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=1.$ So, the first column of $V$ corresponds to the singular value ${\\sigma }_{1}=5.$\n\nHence, we need to find a unit eigenvector of ${A}^{T}\\,A$ that corresponds to ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=25.$ Computing ${A}^{T}\\,A-25I,$ we get\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\,A-25I=[\\begin{aligned}13 & -12 \\\\ -12 & 13\\end{aligned}]-25[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-12 & -12 \\\\ -12 & -12\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-25I)v=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Dividing $v$ by its norm, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|{v}_{11}|+|{v}_{21}|=|-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}|+|\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}|=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$"] [17592186162663 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [17592186161270 :answer-field/correct 17592186161271] ["activity-fb373261-4ba5-5be3-91b7-f2e6612a259f" :activity/id #uuid "fb373261-4ba5-5be3-91b7-f2e6612a259f"] ["step-e41d7701-ae9c-53a9-a74d-30fba5eca257" :step/id #uuid "e41d7701-ae9c-53a9-a74d-30fba5eca257"] ["step-e350249f-f2fe-51bb-bb9e-462f7439d43a" :step/id #uuid "e350249f-f2fe-51bb-bb9e-462f7439d43a"] ["step-df50c27a-eadf-5980-9387-e11247127acf" :step/id #uuid "df50c27a-eadf-5980-9387-e11247127acf"] ["step-da6be4fd-4bca-51c3-b899-c5876bd940c4" :step/id #uuid "da6be4fd-4bca-51c3-b899-c5876bd940c4"] ["step-0469c5e1-c0ea-581f-bb24-0baa86ebe286" :step/id #uuid "0469c5e1-c0ea-581f-bb24-0baa86ebe286"] ["step-e41d7701-ae9c-53a9-a74d-30fba5eca257" :step/content 17592186162663] ["step-e41d7701-ae9c-53a9-a74d-30fba5eca257" :step/next "step-e350249f-f2fe-51bb-bb9e-462f7439d43a"] ["step-e350249f-f2fe-51bb-bb9e-462f743